; expect 42
; A repeat import WIDENS what its module exports. `(import M (alpha))`
; followed by `(import M (beta))` exports both names, not just the
; first list: the module is still merged exactly once (diamond-safe),
; and only the verdicts widen. Before the union, the second list was
; dead text - the module's `beta` stayed unexported and the checker's
; own remedy ("add the name to the import's list", AX3023) was a lie
; the author had already obeyed.
;
;   (alpha 2)  20 - the first list's name, unmoved.
;   (beta 2)   22 - the second list's name, newly exported.
;
; 20 + 22 = 42. A name the module keeps private stays refused when
; named in a second list (still AX3023); that half is probed, not
; pinned, because a case that fails to compile has no exit status.
(import RepeatSel (alpha))
(import RepeatSel (beta))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (if (== (+ (alpha 2) (beta 2)) 42)
    42
    1))
